{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The locking nut assortment felt useful alongside my recent screws, anchors, and framing nails because it adds fastening supplies for repair jobs.",
    "That choice recognized my repeated interest in practical hardware, although it was the only recommendation I would choose now."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Wire gauges, milling cutters, and a lifting sling serve specific tasks I have not shown a need for; buying fasteners does not mean I am doing those jobs.",
    "The hose fitting requires a particular connection and size that my history does not establish, while heat shrink tubing addresses electrical work rather than my recent fastening needs.",
    "Graduated medicine cups do not imply a need for larger glass beakers, and neither baby wipes nor twelve wastebaskets fits a current need.",
    "The caliper is related to hardware, but I have no current need for precise measurements that would make it worth choosing."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in repair supplies seemed to be stretched into an interest in almost any workshop tool or material.",
    "Buying some supplies in bulk seemed to be treated as a reason to recommend large quantities of unrelated products."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated purchases of nails, screws, and anchors make fastening the clearest recurring need in my recent activity.",
    "Specific purpose, dimensions, and compatibility matter more to me than whether something is broadly useful for repairs.",
    "An occasional purchase of measuring cups or vacuum bags does not establish an ongoing need for laboratory equipment or general household supplies."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You partly recognized my need for fastening supplies but extended it to specialized tools and unrelated supplies without a clear current use."
}"}
